# User Blocking System Debug Scratchpad

## 🎯 Objective
Debug and fix the user blocking system that is not working properly, ensuring proper implementation from backend to frontend.

## 🧩 Related Files
1. **Backend Models & Routes**:
   - `backend/models/User.js` - User model with blocking fields (isBlocked, blockInfo schema)
   - `backend/routes/users/admin.js` - Admin routes for block/unblock operations
   - `backend/routes/users/index.js` - User routes including block status check

2. **Android App Files**:
   - `app/src/main/java/com/ds/eventwish/data/remote/ApiService.java` - API endpoints
   - `app/src/main/java/com/ds/eventwish/ui/splash/SplashActivity.java` - Blocking UI implementation
   - `app/src/main/res/layout/dialog_blocked_user.xml` - Blocking dialog UI
   - `app/src/main/java/com/ds/eventwish/utils/EventWishNotificationManager.java` - Notification handling

## ✅ Checklist
1. [ ] Backend Implementation Check:
   - [ ] Verify User model blocking fields and schema
   - [ ] Check block/unblock routes in admin.js
   - [ ] Validate block status check endpoint
   - [ ] Test block status response format

2. [ ] API Integration Check:
   - [ ] Verify ApiService endpoints for block status
   - [ ] Check request/response handling
   - [ ] Validate authentication headers
   - [ ] Test error handling

3. [ ] Frontend Implementation Check:
   - [ ] Review SplashActivity block check flow
   - [ ] Verify blocking dialog implementation
   - [ ] Test notification handling
   - [ ] Check user session management

4. [ ] End-to-End Testing:
   - [ ] Test block operation from admin panel
   - [ ] Verify block status check on app launch
   - [ ] Test blocking dialog display
   - [ ] Verify unblock notification handling

## 🧠 Context
The blocking system involves multiple components working together:
1. Backend stores user blocking status and details
2. Admin routes handle block/unblock operations
3. API endpoints expose block status
4. SplashActivity checks block status on launch
5. UI shows blocking dialog when needed
6. Notifications inform about unblocking

## 🚧 Progress Log
1. Initial Analysis:
   - Backend implementation looks correct
   - API endpoints properly defined
   - Frontend implementation needs review
   - Possible issues in block status check flow

2. Found Issues:
   - [ ] Block status check timing in SplashActivity
   - [ ] Error handling in API calls
   - [ ] Missing admin verification middleware
   - [ ] Notification registration for unblock events

3. Next Steps:
   - Review block status check implementation
   - Add proper error handling
   - Implement admin verification
   - Fix notification registration

# More Category Section Implementation Plan

## 🎯 Objective
Analyze and fix the "More" category section in the HomeFragment and CategoriesAdapter to properly handle category overflow.

